module

public import Theory.SpecificGroups.BabyMonster.Order.LowerBound.ImageSize.Reduction
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.BabyMonster.Order.LowerBound.ImageSize.Conjugacy.RecoveredAData
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.BabyMonster.Order.LowerBound.ImageSize.Conjugacy.RecoveredBData
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.BabyMonster.Order.LowerBound.ImageSize.Conjugacy.QData
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.BabyMonster.Order.LowerBound.ImageSize.Conjugacy.QInvData

/-!
# Concrete candidates for the simultaneous conjugacy certificate

These four binary matrices are decoded from the literal rows generated by the
reproducible computation in `source/`. The algorithm evaluates Table 1 and §3.4
of Breuer–Magaard–Wilson (2019), then compares cyclic bases from corresponding
one-dimensional kernels. The candidates are data only: no word evaluation,
inverse equation, or intertwining equation is asserted by this module.

The row and column convention agrees with `atlasA` and `atlasB`. A separate
certificate must establish `atlasA * conjugacyQ = conjugacyQ * conjugacyA`
and the analogous equation for `atlasB`, together with both inverse products
and the recovered-word evaluations.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace BabyMonster.OrderLowerBound

/-- Candidate value of the first recovered word. -/
def conjugacyA : AtlasMatrix :=
  fun i j => if (conjugacyRecoveredARow i).testBit j.val then 1 else 0

/-- Candidate value of the second recovered word. -/
def conjugacyB : AtlasMatrix :=
  fun i j => if (conjugacyRecoveredBRow i).testBit j.val then 1 else 0

/-- Candidate common intertwiner, using right conjugation. -/
def conjugacyQ : AtlasMatrix :=
  fun i j => if (conjugacyQRow i).testBit j.val then 1 else 0

/-- Candidate inverse of the common intertwiner. -/
def conjugacyQInv : AtlasMatrix :=
  fun i j => if (conjugacyQInvRow i).testBit j.val then 1 else 0

end BabyMonster.OrderLowerBound
